@startuml f9-user-cancel
title F9 - User cancels a task (GW -> State Registry request, EX reports terminal)

|Operator|
start
:Click "Cancel" on task in UI;

|UI|
:Send WS cancel message to API Gateway
 with bearer_token, task_id;

|API Gateway|
:Validate bearer_token;
note right
  GW's only logic.
  Auth + route.
  No connection to Router.
end note
:REST POST /control-requests to State Registry
 with bearer_token, task_id;

|State Registry|
:Append cancel control-request record;
:Append operator audit entry;
:Expose cancel request to assigned Executor;

|EX|
:Read pending cancel request for task_id;

if (Task already running?) then (yes)
  :Terminate task Pod or Docker container;
else (not started yet)
  :Skip starting task runtime;
endif

:REST POST /tasks/:id/status to Router
 with status=cancelled;

|Router|
:Update queue state to cancelled;
:Free occupied slot if any;

|API Gateway|
:Return 200 to UI;

|Operator|
:UI updates task view to "Cancelled";

stop

note right
  UI-originated cancel is a State Registry
  control-request record. The Executor applies it
  for its assigned task and reports terminal status
  back to Router. Router still owns queue state.
end note

@enduml
